### Minimal usage of gsap.matchMedia()

Source: https://gsap.com/docs/v3/GSAP/gsap.matchMedia%28%29

Shows the basic pattern: create a matchMedia instance, add a media query, and define a function that runs when the query matches. Inside, you can create GSAP animations and ScrollTriggers. Optionally return a cleanup function that runs when the query stops matching. All animations and ScrollTriggers created inside are automatically reverted when the query no longer matches.

```javascript
// create
let mm = gsap.matchMedia();

// add a media query. When it matches, the associated function will run
mm.add("(min-width: 800px)", () => {

  // this setup code only runs when viewport is at least 800px wide
  gsap.to(...);
  gsap.from(...);
  ScrollTrigger.create({...});

  return () => { // optional
    // custom cleanup code here (runs when it STOPS matching)
  };
});

// later, if we need to revert all the animations/ScrollTriggers...
mm.revert();
```

--------------------------------

### mm.add()

Source: https://gsap.com/docs/v3/GSAP/gsap.matchMedia%28%29

Adds a media query and a setup function that runs when the query matches. The setup function can optionally return a cleanup function that runs when the query stops matching.

```APIDOC
## mm.add()

### Description
Adds a media query and a setup function. When the media query matches, the setup function runs. When it stops matching, all GSAP animations and ScrollTriggers created during the setup function's execution are reverted automatically. If the setup function returns a function, that function is called as a cleanup when the query stops matching.

### Method
`mm.add(mediaQuery, setupFunction)`

### Parameters
- **mediaQuery** (string) - Required - A media query string, exactly as you would pass to `window.matchMedia()`.
- **setupFunction** (function) - Required - The function to run when the media query matches. It can optionally return a cleanup function.

### Returns
- **MatchMedia** - The MatchMedia instance (for chaining).

### Usage Example
```js
let mm = gsap.matchMedia();
mm.add("(min-width: 800px)", () => {
  gsap.to(...);
  gsap.from(...);
  ScrollTrigger.create({...});
  return () => {
    // custom cleanup code here (runs when it STOPS matching)
  };
});
```

```

