### ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()

Source: https://gsap.com/docs/v3/Plugins/ScrollTrigger/static.matchMedia%28%29

Creates ScrollTriggers that are tied to media queries. Each function is executed when its associated media query matches, and any ScrollTriggers created inside are automatically reverted when the media query no longer matches. The 'all' key runs once and its ScrollTriggers persist.

```APIDOC
## ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()

### Description
Creates ScrollTriggers that are tied to media queries. Each function is executed when its associated media query matches, and any ScrollTriggers created inside are automatically reverted when the media query no longer matches. The 'all' key runs once and its ScrollTriggers persist.

### Method
matchMedia

### Syntax
ScrollTrigger.matchMedia(config)

### Parameters
- **config** (Object) - Required - An object where keys are media query strings (e.g., "(min-width: 960px)") or the special key "all", and values are functions that set up ScrollTriggers.

### Example
```javascript
ScrollTrigger.matchMedia({
  // large
  "(min-width: 960px)": function () {
    // setup animations and ScrollTriggers for screens 960px wide or greater...
    // These ScrollTriggers will be reverted/killed when the media query doesn't match anymore.
  },

  // medium
  "(min-width: 600px) and (max-width: 959px)": function () {
    // The ScrollTriggers created inside these functions are segregated and get
    // reverted/killed when the media query doesn't match anymore.
  },

  // small
  "(max-width: 599px)": function () {
    // The ScrollTriggers created inside these functions are segregated and get
    // reverted/killed when the media query doesn't match anymore.
  },

  // all
  all: function () {
    // ScrollTriggers created here aren't associated with a particular media query,
    // so they persist.
  },
});
```

### Notes
- ScrollTriggers created inside media query functions are automatically reverted/killed when the media query no longer matches.
- ScrollTriggers created inside the "all" function persist regardless of media query.
- Use ScrollTrigger.saveStyles() to record initial inline styles so that reverting works correctly.
```

