### Teardown function example for ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()

Source: https://gsap.com/docs/v3/Plugins/ScrollTrigger/static.matchMedia%28%29

Demonstrates returning a function from a media query callback to clean up non-ScrollTrigger animations when the breakpoint no longer matches. ScrollTrigger automatically kills ScrollTriggers created inside the function, but other animations need manual cleanup.

```javascript
ScrollTrigger.matchMedia({
  // desktop
  "(min-width: 800px)": function () {
    // ScrollTrigger (this automatically gets killed when the breakpoint no longer matches...
    gsap.to(".panel", {
      xPercent: -100,
      scrollTrigger: {
        trigger: ".panel",
        scrub: 1,
        end: "+=500",
      },
    });

    // other animations that aren't ScrollTrigger-related...
    let tl = gsap.timeline();
    tl.to(".box", { rotation: 360 }).to(".box", { y: 100 });

    // THIS IS THE KEY! Return a function that'll get called when the breakpoint no longer matches so we can kill() the animation (or whatever)
    return function () {
      tl.kill();
      // other cleanup code can go here.
    };
  },
});
```
